      "old": "< 2*(sqrt(2))^(q+1)*epsilon.",
      "new": "< 2*(sqrt(2))^(q+1)*epsilon. Since r and epsilon were arbitrary and the remaining branch assumption concerns only n, universally quantify them in this cover-existence conclusion."
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/graph/inferences/@R004/argument/@S004/text",
      "value": "For an arbitrary target scale delta>0, apply the universally quantified construction F003 with its scale parameter equal to min(1,delta/sqrt(2)), which is strictly positive, and with arbitrary positive cost parameter. The resulting covers are delta-covers of F. Let that cost parameter decrease to zero; the multiplier 2*(sqrt(2))^(q+1) is fixed and finite, so H^(q+1)_delta(F)=0. The scale delta was arbitrary, hence H^(q+1)(F)=0. By N001, dim_H(F)<=q+1."
    },
